in-node=3D"105">The Race Condition during Lock Acquisition.</b></p><p data-=
path-to-node=3D"5">If two users call <code data-path-to-node=3D"5" data-ind=
ex-in-node=3D"18">acquireLock()</code> at the exact same millisecond, and y=
our Java code does a "Select then Insert/Update," both might think they suc=
ceeded.</p><h3 data-path-to-node=3D"6">The Fix: Atomic Database Updates</h3=
><p data-path-to-node=3D"7">Don't rely on Java logic to check the lock; let=
 the SQL engine do it. Use a <b data-path-to-node=3D"7" data-index-in-node=
=3D"76">Conditional Update</b> to ensure that lock acquisition is atomic.</=
