n-node=3D"58">Document</code> while the user has the long lock, the <code d=
ata-path-to-node=3D"17,3,0" data-index-in-node=3D"105">@Version</code> will=
 catch it.</p></li></ol><p data-path-to-node=3D"18">This architecture is ef=
fectively a <b data-path-to-node=3D"18" data-index-in-node=3D"35">distribut=
ed state machine</b> implemented inside your RDBMS. It handles the "think t=
ime" of users without holding database connections open.</p><p data-path-to=
-node=3D"19">One thing to keep in mind: you should have a small <b data-pat=
h-to-node=3D"19" data-index-in-node=3D"51">Scheduled Task</b> that deletes =
<code data-path-to-node=3D"19" data-index-in-node=3D"79">IdempotencyRecord<=
/code> entries older than 24 hours to keep that table lean. Would you like =
